    "recommendations": "• Install a reflective address marker at the driveway entrance visible from both directions on the road.\n• Mark the driveway entrance with posts or reflectors to help responders locate the access point quickly at night or in reduced visibility.\n• Widen or clear vegetation along the sides of the driveway to allow large emergency vehicles to pass without obstruction.\n• Designate and mark a turnaround area near the residence so that fire and emergency vehicles can reverse direction without getting stuck.\n• Keep a flat, firm surface available near the residence for ambulance and fire apparatus staging.\n• Trim dense vegetation back from the driveway edge to maintain clear sightlines for drivers of large vehicles navigating the access drive.\n• Install a gate lock box or provide a lockbox code to the local fire department if any gate controls access along the driveway.\n• Mark any soft ground, ditches, or low shoulders along the driveway edge that could cause a heavy vehicle to become stuck.\n• Keep the full length of the driveway clear of parked vehicles, equipment, or debris so responding units can reach the residence without delay.\n• Post a clearly visible address sign at the residence itself, not only at the road, so responders can confirm they have reached the correct structure."
