    "recommendations": "• Trim shrubs that are growing directly against or within a few feet of the house walls.\n• Thin trees closest to the structure to create more open space between the canopy and the roofline.\n• Cut and remove grass around the base of the house before it dries out seasonally.\n• Clear woody debris such as fallen branches, dead wood, and brush piles from around the structure.\n• Remove shrubs growing beneath trees near the house to break up the connection between ground-level plants and tree branches.\n• Thin scattered shrubs along the length of the driveway to keep the travel path clear and visible.\n• Trim any tree branches overhanging the driveway to allow emergency vehicle clearance.\n• Keep the driveway surface free of fallen branches and debris that could block vehicle access.\n• Separate shrub clusters near the house so there are open gaps between individual plants.\n• Move any stored wood piles, yard debris, or flammable materials away from the exterior walls of the house.\n• Remove dead plant material from around any outbuildings or detached structures on the property.\n• Cut grass and low vegetation along both sides of the driveway to maintain clear sightlines and movement along the single access route."
